  {
   "id": "fc466165-9379-41cd-9746-511711c983af",
   "term": "Microphone Polar Patterns Summary",
   "verdict": "MINOR",
   "suggestions": [
    {
     "field": "definition",
     "severity": "Low",
     "issue": "The clause 'all of which become less directional at low frequencies' includes omnidirectional in 'all'. A pressure (omni) pattern cannot become 'less directional' - it is already non-directional at all frequencies (it actually tends to beam/narrow at very high frequencies). Only the directional patterns (cardioid family, figure-8) widen toward omni at low frequencies. The PRACTICAL field already states this correctly ('cardioid becomes more omnidirectional at bass frequencies').",
     "suggestion": "Qualify to the directional patterns, e.g. '...and bidirectional/figure-8 (equal front and back, side nulls) - with the directional patterns (cardioid, super/hyper-cardioid, figure-8) becoming less directional at low frequencies.'"
    }
   ]
